    "badge": "Best Overall Portable Washer",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "1.6 cu ft drum handles a few days of clothes for one or two people",
      "Fully automatic fill, wash, rinse, spin and drain",
      "Quick-connect faucet adapter included per BLACK+DECKER",
      "Multiple cycles and water levels for small or heavy loads",
      "Casters and a compact cabinet make it easy to roll to the sink"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Depends on a faucet that accepts the adapter",
      "Owners commonly report it can walk during spin on uneven floors",
      "Spin leaves clothes wetter than a full-size washer"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The default apartment pick: big enough to matter, small enough to store, and fully automatic once it is hooked up.",
    "description": "The BPWM16W is the portable washer most apartment dwellers should start with. BLACK+DECKER lists it at 1.6 cubic feet, which is the practical sweet spot for one or two people: a few days of clothes, a set of sheets or a handful of towels per load. It is a fully automatic top-loader, so once the inlet hose is clicked onto the faucet adapter and the drain hose is secured in the sink, it fills, washes, rinses, spins and drains without you standing over it. The listing includes several wash cycles and water-level settings, so you are not filling the full drum for a few shirts. Like every small automatic, it is light for its job, and owners commonly report that leveling the feet and balancing loads keeps it from moving during spin. It plugs into an ordinary 120V outlet. Check that your faucet takes a standard aerator-thread adapter before ordering, and budget for a drip pan underneath."
  },
  {
    "id": "black-decker-bpwm09w-portable-washer",
