    "bottomLine": "The automatic to buy when floor space, not load size, is the limit.",
    "description": "The BPWM09W is the smaller sibling of the BPWM16W, listed at 0.9 cubic feet. That is a single-person machine for frequent loads: a day or two of clothes, gym gear or a couple of towels. In exchange, it takes up much less floor space and is light enough to move around easily, which matters in a studio closet, a dorm room or an RV with shore power and a residential-style faucet. It works the same way as the larger model: a quick-connect adapter on the faucet feeds water in, a drain hose goes back to the sink, and the machine handles the whole cycle on its own. Its limitation is obvious. If you wash for two people, or want to do sheets and towels without splitting them across several runs, buy the 1.6 cu ft model instead. If you live alone, wash often and are short on space, the smaller machine is the more sensible buy and one of the easiest to store between uses."
  },
